; Contains modern (2026+) fixes for broken behaviors that probably also existed in the original game
;
; NOUNDEF/ADJDEF must stay at true top level (before any NUMBER/INUMBER block) —
; the parser's room/item sub-loops don't recognize them as block terminators, so
; a NOUNDEF/ADJDEF placed after an open room or item block gets silently dropped.
;
; Reroll charm noun/adjective (see the "reroll charm" item further below).
NOUNDEF 9001 charm
ADJDEF 9001 reroll
;
; Org 14 (Cult of Dahkahn) had two conflicting ORGDEF registrations:
;   - INDOOR.SCR:  ORGDEF 14 INVITE TEMPLE 429 Cult_of_Dahkahn  (room 429 doesn't exist anywhere)
;   - EDDIE3.SCR:  ORGDEF 14 INVITE TEMPLE 65  Cult_of_Dahkahn  (room 65 is "Temple of Shin-jah,
;                  Top Platform" — a different deity's altar, not Dahkahn's)
; Since EDDIE3.SCR loads after INDOOR.SCR and OrgDefs are last-write-wins (keyed by
; org number in engine.go), room 65 was the one actually in effect — so members saw
; a Shin-jah room with no Dahkahn framing when sent to their temple, and (more
; importantly) autoTrainOrgRank's "player.RoomNumber == def.TrainingRoom" check never
; matched real Dahkahn training, since the room that actually carries the
; "---------------Dahkahn training---------------" TRAINING lines (skills 6, 7, 10,
; 12, 14, 23, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30, 32) is room 76, "Dark Cathedral, Chancel" — the room
; with Dahkahn's statue and sacrificial altar, several rooms away from 65. Training
; itself still worked in room 76 (room.TrainingSkills isn't org-gated), but members
; training there could never advance their Cult of Dahkahn rank. Repointing TEMPLE to
; 76, the room the training data actually lives in.
ORGDEF 14 INVITE TEMPLE 76 Cult_of_Dahkahn
;
; Nobody could figure out how to get out of the Rare Weapon Exchange! Changed the door to a normal type
; that you can use GO on (the push door function still works though).
;
NUMBER 345
NAME Rare Weapons Exchange, parlor
INDOOR_GROUND
DEEPCAVE
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
This room is paneled from floor to ceiling in the finest mirmach. Plush leather chairs give the weapons aficionado a place to rest and chat on their favorite subject. On one wall, a portrait of the High Lord of the Crimson Band shows him with a bejeweled greatsword at his side. He was a very big customer of this shop. There is a parchment sign tacked to the wall.
*DESCRIPTION_END
