;
; ISLAND.SCR rooms 2751/2752 (the underwater pools): two bugs.
;
; 1) "GO SURFACE" always failed. Item ref 8 (arch 1597) is the "surface" item
;    the player's GO target actually resolves to, but the surfacing script
;    checked IFPREVERB GO 9 — ref 9 is arch 693 ("ucantsee"), an unrelated
;    hidden placeholder item with no matchable name.
;
; 2) The "you can't hold your breath" auto-surface only worked sporadically
;    (in practice, for whichever player happened to SAY something in the
;    room). The original script raised FLAG1 from many different triggers
;    (SEARCH/WIELD/UNWIELD/PICK/TOUCH/CONCENTRATE/ATTACK/CAST) but checked
;    "IFVAR FLAG1 > 2" as a bare top-level block — the engine only evaluates
;    bare top-level room IFVAR blocks when a player speaks (RunSayScripts);
;    there's no equivalent generic sweep after ordinary commands. So the
;    check was effectively dead except via the room's own IFSAY/ELSE speech
;    handler. Fixed by moving the FLAG1>2 check inline, right after each
;    ADD FLAG1 — each of those triggers already fires reliably through its
;    own verb-specific script runner (RunPreverbScripts/RunRoomVerbScripts),
;    so the check now runs (per-player — FLAG1 is a player field) every time
;    any player's own count crosses the threshold, regardless of other
;    players in the room or of that player ever speaking.
;
; Redefining the rooms whole since the parser replaces same-numbered rooms
; entirely rather than patching individual lines.
;
NUMBER 2751
REGION 11
NAME Pool
CALL 33
ITEM 9 693
*DESCRIPTION_START
Though from above the pool looked dark, some magic allows it to be illuminated to those in the water. The water fills a huge circular chamber with a door in the eastern wall. By going back to the surface, you'll be able to leave the pool.
*DESCRIPTION_END
LIMITED_MOVEMENT
MONSTER_GROUP 63
UNDERSEA
FIXED_LIGHT
ITEM 0 66 CLOSED LOCKED VAL1=60 VAL2=2752 VAL3=3001
ITEM 8 1597
IFVERB SEARCH -1
	ADD FLAG1 1
	IFVAR FLAG1 > 2
		IFVAR RAC < 7
			ECHO PLAYER You can't hold your breath any longer and swim up out of the pool.
			ECHO OTHERS With a stream of bubbles, %N swims to the surface of the pool and gets out.
			AFFECT 2750
				ECHO ALL Out of breath, %N emerges from the pool.
			EQUAL ROUNDTIME 20
			AFFECT 2751
				MOVE 2750
		ENDIF
	ENDIF
	IFVAR SHOOOTER ! TIM
		RANDOM DUMMY1 1 100 0
		ADD DUMMY1 PER
		IFVAR DUMMY1 > 200
			EQUAL SHOOOTER TIM
			NEWITEM 4 1918 ADJ1=1381
			ECHO PLAYER After a careful search, You find some kraken roe.
			ECHO OTHERS %N found something!
		ENDIF
	ENDIF
ENDIF
IFVERB CLOSE 0
	ECHO ALL You hear the click of a lock closing.
	LOCK 0
ENDIF
IFPREVERB TRANSFORM -1
	CLEARVERB
	ECHO PLAYER You are unable to transform in the agitated water.
ENDIF
IFSAY LSJDJWEDYHGKJHDSYEW
	ECHO PLAYER Oh my!
ELSE
	IFVAR RAC < 7
		ECHO PLAYER You open your mouth to speak but lose all your air and have to swim out of the pool.
		ECHO OTHERS With a stream of bubbles, %N swims to the surface of the pool and gets out.
		AFFECT 2751
			ECHO ALL Out of breath, %N emerges from the pool.
		EQUAL ROUNDTIME 20
		AFFECT 2751
			MOVE 2750
	ENDIF
ENDIF
